# MT7925 Crash Report: NULL pointer dereference in mt7925_mac_reset_work
# Date: 2026-01-10 21:31:08 PST
# Kernel: 6.18.4-2-cachyos (CachyOS)
# Hardware: Framework Laptop 16 (AMD Ryzen AI 300 Series)

## Summary

NULL pointer dereference during firmware reset recovery path. The crash occurs
in mt76_connac_mcu_uni_add_dev() when called from mt7925_vif_connect_iter()
during the reset work handler. The vif->bss_conf.chanctx_conf pointer (RSI)
is NULL when accessed.

This is the FOURTH crash today with identical root cause - same bug triggered
during AP roaming when MCU message timeouts lead to firmware reset.

## Root Cause Analysis

The crash occurs because mt7925_vif_connect_iter() iterates over interfaces
during reset recovery, but one or more vifs have been disconnected/disassociated
(chanctx_conf is NULL) before the reset work runs. The code path does not
check for NULL chanctx_conf before passing it to mt76_connac_mcu_uni_add_dev().

Call chain:
  mt7925_mac_reset_work()
    -> ieee80211_iterate_interfaces()
      -> mt7925_vif_connect_iter()
        -> mt76_connac_mcu_uni_add_dev()  <-- crash here, RSI=NULL

